<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. da Vinci returns two weeks after his first visit, six weeks after he slipped on the stone stairs and landed on his bent right elbow. The numbness of the little finger and the inner half of the ring finger and the weakness of the right hand are unchanged; the ring and little fingers still curl when he opens his hand, and he cannot hold the palette or a fine brush. Elbow pain has eased with acetaminophen. He has used a towel around the elbow at night and a gel pad at the drawing table. He has had no new symptoms in the face, speech, vision, legs, or left hand. His home blood pressure readings over a week averaged 127/77 mmHg. He had nerve conduction studies, EMG, and an ultrasound this morning and saw Dr. Lindqvist-Obi of hand surgery afterwards. He draws and writes with his left hand as before. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Six weeks ago, within two days of a fall onto the bent right elbow</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Numb little finger and inner ring finger; weak grip and pinch; curling of the ring and little fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Cannot hold the palette or a fine brush; drawing and writing with the left hand unaffected</td></tr><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Average 127/77 mmHg over seven days</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No face, speech, vision, leg, or left-hand symptoms; no neck pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
