    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1517-08-17; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Neurological, general</td><td>Alert; fluent speech with normal naming; no facial weakness; no pronator drift; NIH Stroke Scale 0; strength, reflexes, and sensation normal in the left arm and both legs; Hoffmann sign absent; plantar responses flexor</td></tr><tr><td>Right arm</td><td>Sensory loss over the little finger, the ulnar half of the ring finger, and the dorsal ulnar hand (two-point discrimination 10 mm at the little finger against 4 mm on the left); first dorsal interosseous 3/5, abductor digiti minimi 3/5, deep flexor of the little finger 4/5, flexor carpi ulnaris 5/5; thumb abduction, wrist and finger extension 5/5; Froment and Wartenberg signs positive; mild clawing of the ring and little fingers; early wasting of the first web space</td></tr><tr><td>Right elbow</td><td>Tinel sign over the cubital tunnel positive; elbow flexion test positive at 30 seconds; nerve does not sublux; full range of motion; bruise resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>Full movement; Spurling test negative</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Regular pulse 70; no carotid bruit; blood pressure 128/78 mmHg</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

